            <ArticleTitle>[Visceral panniculitis in occult pancreatic carcinoma. Case report from clinico-pathologic archives].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe a 75-year-old man with acute abdominal disease leading to lethal prerenal failure. Necropsy revealed massive visceral panniculitis with a small adenocarcinoma of the head of the pancreas. The authors assume that a very rare, early paraneoplastic syndrome was involved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
